---
title: Proposition 5
---
order: 5
---
short_label: IV.5
---
statement: To circumscribe a circle about a given triangle. </font color> <p><b><a href="propIV5.html#cor">Corollary.</a></b> When the center of the circle falls within the triangle, the triangle is acute-angled; when the center falls on a side, the triangle is right-angled; and when the center of the circle falls outside the triangle, the triangle is obtuse-angled.
---
